+# Owned supervisor loss qualification: bounded suspended-only fixture
+
+Base PR60 `ad146eabe2c8ec3cd5028406c737af14c157b808`, tree `31dc88e9a55013fe73da415b79bf07c57fd50b86`; separate feature branch. PR60 source is immutable; only new owned tests/source/design are added here.
+
+## Existing mechanism and scope
+
+GatewayWorker prepares an actual SUSPENDED child in pinned Grid40e9 WindowsJob. Extended limits retain KILL_ON_JOB_CLOSE (0x2000). `_retire_owned` proves empty Job and process exit before closing retained handles on explicit abort. It cannot run Python cleanup after abrupt owner death. A parent must retain independent observation/custody; serialized local snapshots are not authority or adoptable handles.
+
+The old qualify_windows_job script contains ResumeThread/load/memory modes and is NOT imported or executed. PR52 is not included or run. Reuse only primary Grid40e9 WindowsJob cleanup methods and the existing preparation API; no second authority, queue, ledger or publication.
+
+## Plan and safety constraints
+
+1. RED first: add deterministic protocol/rejoin denial tests against a missing new `tests/gateway_jobs/owned_supervisor_loss.py` fixture. Native case is explicitly opt-in, never part of default discovery.
+2. An external watchdog holds an outer kill-on-close Job for the disposable qualification supervisor itself, assigned through its retained process handle before ARM. It verifies direct base-interpreter image/PID/creation identity. The child supervisor has 30s plus <=10s cleanup; external watchdog waits <=40s and reserves the last10s of its total50s budget for actual outer-Job retirement/empty proof. The child creates a private root and an owner interpreter process on retained Popen handles. Owner also blocks on ARM before preparation. Failure/EOF before either ARM exits without worker creation.
+3. Before ARM, create an outer KILL_ON_JOB_CLOSE Job and assign the retained owner process handle directly; no OpenProcess/PID lookup/adoption. Reuse the pinned Grid Job object's terminate-and-wait implementation. Keep outer Job handle noninherited. Thus owner preparation is covered, including the CreateProcess-to-inner-Job interval. Before ARM failure kills only the retained own process.
+4. Owner prepares one suspended child and emits one <=16KiB closed JSON ready frame. Parent uses PeekNamedPipe/available-byte reads with monotonic deadline and size bounds, not unbounded communicate/readline. Child has no inherited handles. No native grant is issued.
+5. Parent duplicates ONLY the prepared process handle from the retained owner process into itself. Verify actual PID/creation FILETIME/image through the duplicate against the own ready record before inducing owner crash. Do not duplicate inner Job: that would defeat last-handle-close behavior. The duplicate permits query/wait and emergency termination of this verified own child only.
+6. Abruptly terminate only the retained own owner process. Observe owner signaled, duplicated child signaled and outer Job ActiveProcesses=0. Normal success must occur from owner-handle loss; if rescue cleanup is needed, fail qualification even if cleanup succeeds. Outer Job remains retained as fallback containment; any uncertain cleanup remains an error, never success.
+7. Start a fresh own owner process under another outer custody Job, with same one-byte ARM gate. Feed only bounded local metadata via a private file. New process incarnation must differ. It must reject old ready/dict/bytes as inspect/abort handles and keep start DENY; no prepare/retry, no PID reopen/adoption. Outcome remains local UNKNOWN, not native job status or hold release.
+8. Absolute nominal scenario budget 30s plus <=10s cleanup. No blocking wait exceeds5s; native wait/read stages use remaining monotonic budget. Cleanup always targets retained own process/Job handles. Remove only verified empty directories/files inside the freshly created private root; no recursive deletion or foreign enumeration.
+9. Record original/source IDs, actual process creation identities, duplicate provenance, current accounting bytes, original failure separately from cleanup errors, retired handles/exit observations, no resume/effect/resource qualification. Source custody is not promoted to production trust. Parent crash closes its outer Job; owner pre-ARM EOF creates no worker.
+10. Run deterministic tests, read-only whole-branch review, then source-bound native case only if these custody/bounds hold without elevation or prohibited diagnostics. Fresh primary pre/post guard, exact HEAD/tree/log/receipt, separate Draft and A8 handoff.
+
+All six resource bounds stay UNSUPPORTED, admitted_fields empty; RSS/commit semantics unchanged. This is an isolated OS owner-loss/rejoin fixture, not distributed restart/lease/fencing acceptance. Actual native job state is UNKNOWN. Public start DENY, INTEGRATION_PENDING / NO-GO.
+
+Review correction before native execution: termination/wait failures previously skipped pipe/process closures. `_retire_owner` now guards termination, wait and every retained close independently. Two new deterministic timeout/deadline/close-fault tests first produced RED, then PASS. Total deterministic fixture tests are five (two protocol/rejoin, two cleanup faults, one image/assignment refusal matrix), not two. Native case remains separately selected. External-watchdog custody was made explicit after ROOT clarification; no qualifier/PR52/Resume/load is used. Inert image/outer-assignment refusals prove no ARM is written; these are not native custody evidence.
+
+First actual exact-source attempt at `15fd084ae2cee131c058ab1db5c8d605b3b3cea8` was RED: 46 local/pure and two prior suspended tests passed; new crash case ERROR, never PASS. Bounded diagnostic reproduction captured FileNotFoundError for Git in the minimized child environment before the core created an owner/worker. Preserve the original protocol error and separate WinError32 directory-cleanup error in external evidence. Confirmed both private failure directories were empty and subsequently retired with nonrecursive rmdir.
+
+Correction: use an absolute discovered Git path for primary reads and retain only that executable's directory in child PATH. Record Git executable path/SHA256; this is diagnostic provenance, not trusted source qualification. Structured child failures and bounded unexpected-frame capture retain original diagnostics. Verified-directory rmdir retries only Windows32/145 within the existing cleanup deadline, never silently accepts an error. Watchdog retains its outer Job until process and filesystem cleanup finishes, after actual zero-active accounting. Added environment and bounded-directory regression tests: fixture deterministic count is now seven. Re-review before the next native attempt; no mass retry or relaxation.
+
+ROOT follow-up tightens empty-directory retries: each attempt rechecks same ordinary-directory identity, rejects reparse points and freshly confirms empty; nonempty stops immediately. No content deletion is performed by the retry helper. Stderr is a separate bounded pipe and is never parsed as a protocol frame. Supervisor errors are structured; owner/restart errors can still be captured as bounded traceback diagnostics, not valid frames. No live/private inputs exist in this fixture: it uses the committed FORMAT_ONLY synthetic request and minimized environment only.
+
+A deterministic pipe-exit race also reproduced RED: data written immediately before process exit must be drained within the same deadline, rather than rejected merely because the retained process became signaled. This race, stderr separation and nonempty-directory rejection now have RED/GREEN tests. Current deterministic fixture count is ten (not seven); the actual crash case remains a separate test. Only source files changed since the failed native attempt; the next actual attempt requires reviewed, fresh exact committed source.
